Subject: [PATCH] luci-app-passwall2: group subscription nodes by region while updating

A subscription with region grouping enabled gets its nodes created in their
region group directly, in the same uci call that creates them, so no node is
written twice. The name of the subscription is kept in sub_src.

Everything in subscribe.lua that used the group of a node to find the nodes of
a subscription now uses the subscription (sub_src, otherwise group): the
deletion of the old nodes, the five matching tiers that keep references to
nodes (shunt rules, load balancing, ...) after an update, and "delete the
subscribed nodes". The region settings are part of the subscription MD5, so a
changed setting is applied by the next update. Balancing nodes are synced after
the nodes are created, and the config is backed up right before the commit.
---
